      "harm": "using an atomic counter for cursor synchronization is non-standard and less suitable than a shared mutex",
      "quote": "I'm not sure about this approach with an atomic counter though. Would it make sense to instead have a shared mutex that would allow multiple consumers to take a read lock along with the cursor, which are then released in the destructor?",
      "blocking": false,
      "status": "resolved",
